<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Access WiFi Information. NEHotspotNetwork.fetchCurrent needs this (plus
       Location permission, requested via NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription in
       Info.plist.in) to return the current SSID and signal strength. Without
       both, fetchCurrent yields nil: the file transfer screen cannot name the
       network or draw signal bars, and WiFiClass falls back to reporting
       WIFI_SCAN_FAILED, which lands the owner on the manual SSID entry list.
       Degraded, not broken. But the point of this entitlement is that the phone
       can tell the truth about the network it is on.

       THIS MUST BE ENABLED ON THE APP ID before a device build will sign.
       Apple Developer, then Certificates / Identifiers / Profiles, then the
       app's identifier, then Access WiFi Information. Automatic signing fails
       with a provisioning profile mismatch otherwise, which reads as a
       certificate problem rather than as a missing capability.

       Applied only to device builds; see ios/CMakeLists.txt. The iOS Simulator
       neither needs it nor honours it, since fetchCurrent returns nil there
       regardless. That is why this path can only be QA'd on real hardware. -->
  <key>com.apple.developer.networking.wifi-info</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
